  "title": "Battle of Salamis",
  "summary": "In September 480 BCE the allied Greek fleet defeated the Persian navy in the strait of Salamis, opposite Athens. Livius says at least a third of the Persian ships were defeated by nightfall and that Xerxes recalled his army, a serious setback but not a disaster; the Greeks and Persians met again at Plataea in 479 BCE.",
